 "observations": [
  "The page number «185» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 71», in bold sans serif, underlined. At the foot, the signature line of the printed sheet: «D. K. D. Vidensk. Selsk. Skr., 7. Række, hist. og filos. Afd. III. 1.» on the left and the sheet number «24» on the right; recorded here, not transcribed as a line. The titles (L01-L02), in bold, the sigla in roman: N's «Tabula coniunctionis et oppositionis in annis arabum residuis (N)» and that of C and O, «Gedval coniunctionis et oppositionis in annis arabum planis (CO)». The folios of the manuscripts stand at the right of the second title in two lines, «C 82r, O 139r,» and «N 43v.», the letters raised; here as right margin notes beside L01 and L02.",
  "The table: eighteen columns divided by double vertical rules: «Notulae1)» and «Dies subtrahendi», printed upwards, «Anni plani2)», «Horae» over «Horae», «Min.», «Sec.», and «Medium3) solis et lunae», «Argumentum lunae» and «Argumentum latitudinis», each over «Sig.», «Gr.», «Min.», «Sec.»; the units in smaller bold type. Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L03-L05); the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The range of note e is marked at its first and last rows, 2 and 30 (L07, L35).",
  "L06-L35. The rows are the single years 1-30, whose values are added to a row of Tab. 69 or Tab. 70 (pp. 183-184) for the conjunction or the opposition; Suter's example adds the row of 17 (L22), 5h 43m 50s, 5s 27° 30′ 35″, 7s 16° 38′ 40″ and 4s 16° 48′ 10″ (p. 82, JP2 0114, L24), and the 8h 48m 7s of the year 1 (L06) is quoted on p. 82, L05. The time is the excess of 12 synodic months a year over the days of the years, 354 in a common year and 355 in the leap years 2, 5, 7, 10, 13, 16, 18, 21, 24, 26 and 29 of Tab. 2 (p. 110, JP2 0142); where the months fall short of the days, a day is subtracted and 24 hours are added. Checked: the column «Dies subtrahendi» has 1 in exactly these rows; the times follow p · 8h 48m 27.1s less the leap days (0h 13m 33s at 30) within 10s in every row except at 1, 4, 5, 21 and 29: with 27, 13 and 36 for the printed 7, 53 and 56 the first, the second and the fourth agree (see the critical notes); at 5, 20h 15m 14s, the law gives 20h 2m 15s, and at 29, 15h 29m 22s, it gives 15h 25m 6s.",
  "L06-L35, continued. Checked: the mean longitude is p · 11s 19° 15′ 55″, the motion of the sun in 12 synodic months, to the second in every row except at 3, 5, 6, 7 and 24 (see the critical notes); 1s 7° 57′ 30″ at 30, 7″ less than the 1s 7° 57′ 37″ by which Tab. 69 grows in 30 collected years. The anomaly is p · 10s 9° 48′ 9.6″ within 7″ in every row except at 3, 7, 8, 16, 28 and 30 (see the critical notes) and at 4 and 19, 5s 9° 12′ 29″ and 4s 6° 14′ 48″, 9″ and 14″ less; 9s 24° 4′ 48″ at 30 is 7″ less than the 9s 24° 4′ 55″ of Tab. 69. The argument of latitude is p · 8° 2′ 50″ to the second in every row except at 22 (see the critical note); 8s 1° 25′ 0″ at 30 is 22″ less than the 8s 1° 25′ 22″ of Tab. 69.",
  "L06-L35, «Notulae». The weekday numbers grow by 4 a common year and by 5 a leap year, counted 1-7, from 2 at the year 1; all thirty as printed, with the readings of notes a-d. Each is one more than the nota of the following year in Tab. 2 (p. 110).",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the same laws: the edition's readings are those of the regular values at 2, 23, 26 and 29 in the first column (notes a-d: C's 7 against O's 6, O's 7 against C's 4 and 3, the 6 of O and N against C's 5), at 1 and 7 in the time (notes f and g: C's 8 against O's 7, the 39 of O and N against C's 29, 13h 39m 9s by the law), and in the argument of latitude at 30 (note h, N's sign 8 against the 7 of C and O), 10 (note i, the minutes 28 of C and O against N's 18) and 16 (note k, N's seconds 20 against the 4 of C and O). Note e, marked at 2 and 30 («e)—e)»): O omits the even years 2-30.",
  "Notes 1-3: «Notulae» (C and N), O's «Notae»; «plani» (C and O), N's «residui», the remaining years; C's «elwacat», al-wasaṭ, the mean, for «Medium». Italics: «numeros pares om.»."
 ],
